{
  "_comment": [
    "The sample games an install ships so a fresh AutoBleem is not an empty shelf: homebrew whose licence lets us",
    "redistribute it (every entry names it), one per system at least. tools/build_samples.py downloads each file",
    "from its upstream release (sha256-checked), lays it out as it lands on the data partition and packs",
    "samples-<date>.tar.gz for the download repository (samples/); payload_rpi/install.sh fetches that.",
    "The PS1 game gets a locked Game.ini (Automation=0) so the scanner keeps the metadata and the cover written",
    "here, and a pcsx.cfg - 'skip_boot_logo' sets SlowBoot = 0 in it, for a disc whose custom boot logo breaks",
    "pcsx-ab's BIOS shell; the ROMs are named as the launcher's ROM scan labels them (the file's stem) with a box art of the",
    "same name in the thumbnails tree. Covers: tools/samples/make_covers.py -> covers/ (checked in).",
    "'shot' is the screenshot make_covers.py draws from (a file under tools/samples/shots/, from the game's own",
    "repository, under the game's licence)."
  ],
